Frozen predecessor-writer fixture for #10637: a save taken by the base engine
at the CR 903.9b commander choice under Hallowed Burial, with the commander
(Otrimi, the Ever-Playful) merged over Gemrazer, after the owner submitted the
order of the two components. Checked restore on the current engine must refuse
it with PersistedRestoreError::UnresumableSharedBatchPause.

Generated by the OLD serializer. Never regenerate it with a newer engine: its
value is that it is byte-for-byte what the predecessor engine wrote.

Generating commit: bea11941d4cbde87947d949855796426690b9680
  (upstream phase-rs/phase main, v0.122.0; #10637's merge base before
  c53dd8a81, which changed only crates/phase-ast data)

Serializer: PersistedGameState::capture(state) after state.capture_rng_word_pos(),
  pretty-printed with serde_json::to_string_pretty plus a trailing newline.

Command (bash, on minto-3, in a clean worktree checked out at the commit above,
with the generator below added as
crates/engine/tests/integration/zz_base_9039b_fixture_gen.rs and a matching
`mod zz_base_9039b_fixture_gen;` line in shard_5.rs):

  CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/storage/targets/pr10637-wrangle-base CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 \
  FIXTURE_DIR=/tmp/pr10637-gen \
  cargo test -p phase-engine --test integration_5 generate_base_9039b_fixtures -- --nocapture

One run writes both fixtures (base_9039b_merged_hallowed.json and
base_9039b_hallowed_order.json). Observed on that run (the predecessor's own
behaviour after declining the command zone, live and after restoring its own
save, is part of the record):

  GEN[merged] ids host=ObjectId(2) rider=ObjectId(3) burial=ObjectId(4) library=[ObjectId(1)] battlefield=[ObjectId(2), ObjectId(3)] hand=[ObjectId(4)]
  GEN[merged] owner order prompt lists [ObjectId(3), ObjectId(2)]
  GEN[merged] submitted [ObjectId(3), ObjectId(2)]; paused at ReplacementChoice ["Move to command zone", "Put into library"]; library [ObjectId(1), ObjectId(3)]
  GEN[merged] FIXTURE written to /tmp/pr10637-gen/base_9039b_merged_hallowed.json (107474 bytes)
  GEN[merged] base live decline: PANICKED
  GEN[merged] base restored decline: PANICKED
  GEN[order] ids host=ObjectId(2) rider=ObjectId(3) burial=ObjectId(4) library=[ObjectId(1)] battlefield=[ObjectId(2), ObjectId(3)] hand=[ObjectId(4)]
  GEN[order] owner order prompt lists [ObjectId(3), ObjectId(2)]
  GEN[order] submitted [ObjectId(3), ObjectId(2)]; paused at ReplacementChoice ["Move to command zone", "Put into library"]; library [ObjectId(1), ObjectId(3)]
  GEN[order] FIXTURE written to /tmp/pr10637-gen/base_9039b_hallowed_order.json (95623 bytes)
  GEN[order] base live decline: library [ObjectId(1), ObjectId(3), ObjectId(2)], then Priority { player: PlayerId(0) }
  GEN[order] base restored decline: library [ObjectId(1), ObjectId(3), ObjectId(2)], then Priority { player: PlayerId(0) }

The panics are the predecessor's own assertion at
crates/engine/src/game/zone_pipeline.rs:1716 (bea11941d): "resumed batch member
2 (incarnation 0) has no terminal completion (0 retained delivery events)".

Infrastructure exception: the merged board uses
engine::game::merge::merge_object_onto(rider, host, MergeSide::Bottom) in place
of Gemrazer's public mutate cast, as the existing Hallowed Burial rows in
owner_library_arrangement_simultaneity.rs do.

Generator source:

//! Scratch generator for #10637's frozen predecessor-writer fixtures. Not for commit.
//! Run on a clean worktree of bea11941d (v0.122.0) as
//! crates/engine/tests/integration/zz_base_9039b_fixture_gen.rs with a matching
//! `mod zz_base_9039b_fixture_gen;` line in shard_5.rs.

use engine::game::scenario::{GameRunner, GameScenario, P0};
use engine::types::actions::GameAction;
use engine::types::game_state::{PersistedGameState, WaitingFor};
use engine::types::identifiers::ObjectId;
use engine::types::mana::{ManaType, ManaUnit};
use engine::types::phase::Phase;

const HALLOWED_BURIAL: &str = "Put all creatures on the bottom of their owners' libraries.";
const OTRIMI: &str = "Mutate {1}{B}{G}{U} (If you cast this spell for its mutate cost, put it over or under target non-Human creature you own. They mutate into the creature on top plus all abilities from under it.)\nTrample\nWhenever this creature deals combat damage to a player, return target creature card with mutate from your graveyard to your hand.";
const GEMRAZER: &str = "Mutate {1}{G}{G} (If you cast this spell for its mutate cost, put it over or under target non-Human creature you own. They mutate into the creature on top plus all abilities from under it.)\nReach, trample\nWhenever this creature mutates, destroy target artifact or enchantment an opponent controls.";

/// Otrimi (commander, object 2) and Gemrazer (object 3) on P0's battlefield,
/// "Sentinel" (object 1) on top of P0's library, Hallowed Burial (object 4).
fn board(merged: bool) -> (GameRunner, ObjectId, ObjectId, ObjectId) {
    let mut scenario =
        GameScenario::new_with_format(engine::types::format::FormatConfig::commander(), 2, 42);
    scenario.at_phase(Phase::PreCombatMain);
    scenario.with_mana_pool(
        P0,
        [
            ManaType::White,
            ManaType::White,
            ManaType::Colorless,
            ManaType::Colorless,
            ManaType::Colorless,
        ]
        .into_iter()
        .map(|color| ManaUnit::new(color, ObjectId(0), false, vec![]))
        .collect(),
    );
    scenario.with_library_top(P0, &["Sentinel"]);
    let host = scenario
        .add_creature_from_oracle(P0, "Otrimi, the Ever-Playful", 6, 6, OTRIMI)
        .as_legendary()
        .with_subtypes(vec!["Nightmare", "Beast"])
        .commander()
        .id();
    let rider = scenario
        .add_creature_from_oracle(P0, "Gemrazer", 4, 4, GEMRAZER)
        .with_subtypes(vec!["Beast"])
        .id();
    let burial = scenario
        .add_spell_to_hand_from_oracle(P0, "Hallowed Burial", false, HALLOWED_BURIAL)
        .with_mana_cost(engine::types::mana::ManaCost::Cost {
            shards: vec![
                engine::types::mana::ManaCostShard::White,
                engine::types::mana::ManaCostShard::White,
            ],
            generic: 3,
        })
        .id();
    let mut runner = scenario.build();
    if merged {
        // Stand-in for Gemrazer's mutate resolving under Otrimi.
        engine::game::merge::merge_object_onto(
            runner.state_mut(),
            rider,
            host,
            engine::game::merge::MergeSide::Bottom,
            &mut Vec::new(),
        );
    }
    (runner, host, rider, burial)
}

fn library(runner: &GameRunner) -> Vec<ObjectId> {
    runner.state().players[0].library.iter().copied().collect()
}

fn generate(label: &str, merged: bool, out: &str) {
    let (mut runner, host, rider, burial) = board(merged);
    println!(
        "GEN[{label}] ids host={host:?} rider={rider:?} burial={burial:?} library={:?} battlefield={:?} hand={:?}",
        library(&runner),
        runner.state().battlefield,
        runner.state().players[0].hand
    );
    let outcome = runner.cast(burial).resolve();
    let WaitingFor::EffectZoneChoice { cards, .. } = outcome.final_waiting_for().clone() else {
        panic!("GEN[{label}] expected the owner's order first: {:?}", outcome.final_waiting_for());
    };
    println!("GEN[{label}] owner order prompt lists {cards:?}");
    // Submit Gemrazer above Otrimi: the reverse of battlefield (announcement) order.
    let submitted = vec![rider, host];
    runner
        .act(GameAction::SelectCards { cards: submitted.clone() })
        .expect("the owner submits an order");
    let WaitingFor::ReplacementChoice { candidates, .. } = runner.state().waiting_for.clone() else {
        panic!("GEN[{label}] expected the CR 903.9b choice: {:?}", runner.state().waiting_for);
    };
    println!(
        "GEN[{label}] submitted {submitted:?}; paused at ReplacementChoice {:?}; library {:?}",
        candidates.iter().map(|c| c.description.clone()).collect::<Vec<_>>(),
        library(&runner)
    );
    let state = runner.state_mut();
    state.capture_rng_word_pos();
    let json = serde_json::to_string_pretty(&PersistedGameState::capture(state.clone()))
        .expect("state serializes");
    std::fs::write(out, format!("{json}\n")).expect("fixture written");
    println!("GEN[{label}] FIXTURE written to {out} ({} bytes)", json.len() + 1);

    // What the predecessor engine itself does next: live, and after restore.
    for (mode, start) in [
        ("live", runner.state().clone()),
        (
            "restored",
            serde_json::from_str::<PersistedGameState>(&json)
                .expect("base decodes its own save")
                .into_game_state()
                .expect("base restores its own save"),
        ),
    ] {
        let finished = std::panic::catch_unwind(std::panic::AssertUnwindSafe(|| {
            let mut next = GameRunner::from_state(start);
            next.act(GameAction::ChooseReplacement { index: 1 })
                .expect("decline the command zone");
            (library(&next), next.state().waiting_for.clone())
        }));
        match finished {
            Ok((library, waiting)) => {
                println!("GEN[{label}] base {mode} decline: library {library:?}, then {waiting:?}")
            }
            Err(_) => println!("GEN[{label}] base {mode} decline: PANICKED"),
        }
    }
}

#[test]
fn generate_base_9039b_fixtures() {
    let dir = std::env::var("FIXTURE_DIR").expect("FIXTURE_DIR set");
    generate("merged", true, &format!("{dir}/base_9039b_merged_hallowed.json"));
    generate("order", false, &format!("{dir}/base_9039b_hallowed_order.json"));
}
